# LF everywhere, including on a Windows checkout.
#
# Not a style preference: the assets under `assets/` are embedded with
# `include_str!` and shipped into a project byte for byte, so a checkout that
# rewrote them to CRLF would build a binary that installs CRLF files — and the
# tests that read those bytes back (`install::tests`, which asserts a skill
# opens with `---\n`) would fail on that machine and nowhere else. The shell
# scripts under `scripts/` cannot survive CRLF at all.
#
# Git for Windows sets `core.autocrlf=true` system-wide, so without this file
# the Windows CI job checks out a tree no other job sees.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
